[Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  this week i'm trying something kind of  different  apple sent me the new iphone 13 pro to  review and i've been roaming around the  north cascades in washington seeing what  this phone can do some of you have asked  about my camera setup and while i do use  my canon r5 and lenses for most  landscape scenes at least half of what  you see here on my youtube channel is  shot with my iphone  so thought it would be fun to film a  review of this phone out here on the  road and share my overall thoughts from  a photographer's perspective  this isn't a deep dive on technical  specs mostly i just want to show you  what this phone can do from a visual  standpoint  like they say the best camera is the one  you have with you  [Music]  so  [Music]  do  [Music]  hmm  [Music]  do  [Music]  i'm driving on the north cascades  highway right now and the fall colors  are so beautiful  it's pretty rainy out but um  yeah so i'm getting this shot by holding  out my right hand  holding the iphone  and  it's pretty stable i think i guess we'll  find out but  yeah this is a front-facing camera so  quality seems pretty good  and i have no idea how the audio will  sound but  especially with the road noise and the  rain  but i guess we'll find out together  so  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  oh  wow this is so cool do you know what  kind of salmon these are  so these are salmon  and they're coming up stream to spawn  and they've lived their whole lives out  at sea  how cool is that  so  look outside  [Music]  painted skies here comes the light  it's in your eyes  [Music]  fear  [Music]  this  [Music]  oh this view is incredible  so  this is cinematic mode and you can see  it's blurring the background here  the way a prime lens would blur the  background  which is pretty incredible for an iphone  it's uh  pretty awesome to be able to  just take a phone up into the mountains  and get this kind of quality video  but check out this view  [Music]  is  everything  [Music]  made it up to the top  this view  is ridiculous  oh that was super crooked  um and this is cinematic mode so you can  see there's a little bit of blur in the  background here which is nice and yeah  it was a little bit of a slog up that  last bit but now it's getting chilly so  put on all the layers  and  yeah overall this phone is pretty  spectacular there's a few different  talking points i want to go over stuff  that you know i've been using it for  about two weeks now and stuff i want to  mention that i can't remember up here on  the mountain top plus it's about to get  dark soon so we should probably hike  down because we got four three and a  half or four miles we're not sure to get  back down to  the vehicles gonna have to get a move on  but i will talk to you about the phone  when i'm back at the van all right so  it's 7 30  and it's already  basically  pretty much night time  and you can also use your iphone  as headlamp  photography slash hiking multi-tool  we are back in the van and i am filming  this on the iphone 13 pro okay so i've  had this phone for about two weeks now  and there are a couple of things that  have really stood out to me first is the  battery life i've noticed that i'm  reaching for my cord way less often than  i have in the past and in some instances  i've even gone a whole day without  having to charge my phone at all so  being on the road or if you live a  mobile lifestyle or any lifestyle really  just not having to charge your phone as  often is amazing it's definitely a nice  upgrade second the one terabyte storage  option is a game changer that's what  this phone is and i was able to film  this entire vlog without having to stop  and offload or delete files or anything  like that which really allowed me to  stay in the creative mindset throughout  the entire filming process  and what's also nice is you can go  through and review each individual clip  you can scrub through you can trim you  can delete before you drop those files  over into your editing timeline and the  fact that you can do that natively on  the phone while filming i could just see  how this would save me so much time in  the editing process moving forward also  stabilization is better low light  capture is better these cameras actually  have a wider aperture than the iphone  pro 12 which means less noise overall um  that clip that i just showed you where i  was walking through the dark without a  headlamp but filming it you could see  how dark it was and when i took this  photo this was taken three seconds hand  held no tripod  and you can still see some light in  there which is remarkable for a mobile  device with the pro the cinematic macro  and 77 millimeter modes have been really  fun to experiment with it uses digital  blur so there are some instances where  you can you know see that it's not  perfect if you zoom in but it's still  really incredible technology and it's a  small price to pay when you consider how  much you would have to spend and invest  into a camera and the lenses and all of  the things and also how heavy that stuff  is like when i lug my camera and lenses  up onto a mountain top  oh i mean in some sometimes it gets as  heavy as 12 pounds the iphone obviously  weighs a fraction of that and it costs  less and it's multifunctional you know  you use your phone for so many things  and it just so happens to be an  excellent vlogging camera that being  said if you already have the iphone 11  or 12 or any of the pro models you  already have an incredible device in  your pocket i use the iphone 12 pro for  the past year i absolutely loved it in  fact i use it to film at least 50 of  what you've seen on this channel like i  said earlier so  there's no need to upgrade but if you  are looking for something that really  kicks it up a notch and they can kind of  take your content to the next level  without investing in all of that camera  gear this is it let me know if you guys  like this video and if you'd like to see  more gear based reviews in the future i  had a lot of fun filming this one with  nathaniel wise who is also an outdoor  adventure photographer if you aren't  following him already definitely go  check out his channel also i'm leaving  for europe in a couple days i'm super  excited i'll be over there for about  three weeks with some friends and i'll  be going to italy and switzerland for  sure and potentially france and austria  not totally sure yet but if you'd like  to see some mountain content  fall colors  um really good food and just general  whatever we get up to in europe  subscribe  and if not don't worry about it  um and also like and comment this video  if you want to but either way i  appreciate you being here thank you and  i'll see you guys next time  [Music]  should you get me coming out of the  toilet

